WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.120
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.340
Today, I’m going to explain an episode called
“The H0unds 0f Baskervi11e” from the Mystery

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.080
Crime show “Sherlock.”

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.550
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:10.983
Watch out and take care!

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.360
At the beginning of the episode, we see a
little boy running up a hill through the woods.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.230
He looks frantic and scared.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.460
An old lady stops the kid, and asks if he
is okay.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.050
The boy doesn’t say anything but yells in
fear.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.449
The child’s name is Henry Knight.

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:33.079
Cut to twenty years later; Henry has grown
up into an adult.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:35.420
He stands in the same woods in Dartmoor.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.290
It turns out that 20 years ago, he had seen
his father got killed by a gigantic hound.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.390
The incident has traumatized Henry for life.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.250
Somewhere else in London, a detective named
Sherlock Holmes and his partner, John Watson,

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:49.713
are in their apartment.

00:00:49.713 --> 00:00:52.313
Sherlock comes in with a weapon and blood
all over him.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.720
He has just solved another case.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.070
Sherlock is experiencing withdrawal; He has
to solve cases to keep him from smoking.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.680
He throws stuff around the apartment, looking
for his secret stash of cigarettes and yelling

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.540
at John to find a case.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.670
Just then, their doorbell rings.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.030
In comes Henry.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.570
He wants Sherlock to investigate the case
of his father’s death.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:16.690
He and his father used to go for walks to
moor; the woods has a place called Dewer’s Hollow

00:01:17.135 --> 00:01:21.818
That day, a massive animal had caught Henry’s
father; it dragged and killed him in front of Henry

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:27.390
He brings a news report on Baskerville, a
chemical and biological weapons research centre

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.659
in Dartmoor.

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:32.790
He's convinced that a monster brewed in the
Baskerville lab killed his father.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:37.189
However, Sherlock believes that Henry has
just created a story to cope with his trauma,

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:38.990
so he dismisses him.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.810
But just then, Henry tells him that after
years of trauma, yesterday, Henry has visited

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:48.430
the hollow where the killing occurred, and
found gigantic paw prints of a hound.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:52.040
The fact that Henry called it a ‘hound’
instead of a ‘dog’ spikes Sherlock’s  interest.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.949
So he and John leave for Dartmoor the following
morning.

00:01:55.509 --> 00:01:59.501
The two check into a hotel ,and on their way,
see a tour guide boasting about the hound

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.229
to a group of tourists.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.590
The hound had become a local legend, and helped
to grow the place’s tourism.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:09.360
Meanwhile, Henry is at his therapist, Louise
Mortimer’s home.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.330
This time, during the session, he reveals
to her that he sees the words ‘liberty’

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.610
and ‘in’, in relation to the night his
father was killed.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.470
While checking into the hotel, John sees a
receipt of a large amount of meat supplied

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.760
to the hotel.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.660
Thinking it is unusual, he takes the bill
with him.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.819
The two then talk to the tour guide, who tells
them that he has seen the hound too.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:33.510
He believes that the Ministry of Defence research
base, called the Baskerville created the hound,

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.860
as a defense mechanism during the war.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.230
Ever since, the hound has been running around
in Dartmoor killing people.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.239
The two then visit Baskerville.

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:45.620
They use Sherlock’s brother, Mycroft’s
security pass to get access into the building.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.120
However, the establishment is highly protected,
so they have only about twenty minutes before

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.709
they get caught.

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:54.800
One of the guards there offers the two a full
tour of the place.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.380
They meet a lab doctor named Dr. Bob Frankland
while touring.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.910
They walk around the labs, but do not find
any useful information about the hound, before

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.500
Mycroft’s card causes a security alert.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.569
The major is about to run an identity check
on them when suddenly, Dr Frankland claims

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:12.480
to know him, and backs up Sherlock's ruse.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.970
Turns out Franklin is a fan of Sherlock's
work, and he knows Henry and knew that they

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.660
came to help him.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:22.200
Frankland says he was a friend of Henry's
father and is concerned for Henry's well-being.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.120
The duo then visits Henry’s home in Dartmoor.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.200
Henry offers them some tea, and tells them
of the words that he keeps seeing in his dreams,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.540
“liberty” and “in”.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.659
Sherlock’s next plan is to visit the Dewer’s
Hollow at night, and investigate the presence

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:35.880
of the hound.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.920
The three make their way to the place in the
evening that day.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.690
As they walk, John hears a noise coming from
the bushes behind him.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.590
He separates from the group and investigates
the noise.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:48.629
There, he sees a light flashing from far away.

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:51.610
It looks like someone is trying to communicate
in morse code.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:55.349
John looks behind to call Sherlock, but they
have already walked far.

00:03:55.349 --> 00:03:59.500
John decodes the morse, and finds that it
is saying “U-M-Q-R-A”.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.470
Unsure of what that means, he goes back looking
for Sherlock and Henry.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:08.220
The other two have already reached the Dewer’s
hollow; Sherlocks goes inside the pit to check.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.110
As he looks around, he sees a massive animal
on the edge of the pit.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.299
Henry sees it too.

00:04:13.299 --> 00:04:17.840
Nervous, Henry comes running to Sherlock...
asking if he saw it too.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.430
The two then get out of the pit and meet John.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.740
Henry tells John that they saw the hound,
but Sherlock insists that he did not.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.560
Henry is frustrated by Sherlock’s denial;
he is sure that Sherlock saw it too and is

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.169
happy to find that he did not make the hound
up.

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:34.610
Later, John and Sherlock are in a restaurant.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.650
Sherlock doesn’t talk and looks nervous.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.530
As John tells him about the morse code, Sherlock
interrupts him to tell him that he actually

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.110
saw the hound too.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.310
He denied seeing it earlier to hide the fact
that he was scared.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.003
John tries calming him, suggesting he is imagining
things.

00:04:49.003 --> 00:04:52.783
Sherlock reacts with anger, insisting that
he is in a good mental state.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.780
The two get into a fight, after which John
walks away from him.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:01.290
Outside the restaurant, he sees the same morse
code blinking far away in the hills.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.139
He sets off to look for the source.

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:07.740
Finally, he finds that they were just headlights
from flashes from a group of doggers.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.650
Embarrassed, he returns back.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.120
Henry is back home when he suddenly wakes
up at night.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.750
Suddenly, he starts to hallucinate the night
his father was killed.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.430
He sees the words ‘liberty’ and ‘in’
repeatedly.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:23.240
He tries watching TV ,but every show has some
kind of dog in it.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.160
Suddenly, the out light turns on and off.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.670
Henry gets his gun out.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.840
Just then there is a bang on the glass door.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.700
The lights start to flicker again.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.320
Scared, he falls to the floor.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.007
The following day, Sherlock makes John go
on a date with Henry’s therapist, Louise Mortimer.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:43.570
John tries getting information out of her
without revealing his true intention.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.770
The pair share a flirty drink as they chat
about Baskerville and the hound, but Dr Franklin

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.750
ruins the mood when he exposes John as a professional
investigator.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.050
Louise leaves right after.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:57.080
The following morning, Sherlock goes to Henry’s
home.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.770
He is overly excited which sets Henry off.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:03.240
He has not slept in days because of his night
terrors.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:06.690
Sherlocks directly runs to the kitchen to
make himself a coffee, and starts looking

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:08.320
through the cabinets.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:12.810
Henry asks him why he denied seeing the hound
the other day, but Sherlock dismisses it.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.900
Instead, he questions Henry why the creature
is called ‘Hound’.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.210
Before he can let Henry answer, Sherlock abruptly
leaves the place and sees John writing something

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.750
on his notepad.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.500
While talking, Sherlock realizes something.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.419
He suggests that the word hound is actually
an acronym that stands for something.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:32.669
John is confused but goes with his friend’s
theory.

00:06:32.669 --> 00:06:37.039
Just then, Sherlock runs into DI Lestrade,
who he suspects has been sent to Dartmoor

00:06:37.039 --> 00:06:38.539
by his brother Mycroft.

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:43.170
Meanwhile, John reveals a clue he discovered
earlier - inside the inn where he and Sherlock

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:47.660
are staying, is a receipt for a large delivery
of meat, even though the bar and restaurant

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.509
is strictly vegetarian.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:54.110
The innkeeper admits that he briefly kept
a wild dog on the moor - disguising it as the famous hound

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.750
to boost tourism.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:59.741
However, he insists that the creature's been
put down a month ago, and in any case, it

00:06:59.741 --> 00:07:04.480
bears little resemblance to the monstrous
creature that Sherlock and Henry encountered...

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.749
After that, Sherlock claims that he has a
theory, but has to go to Baskerville to test it.

00:07:09.463 --> 00:07:13.033
They cannot pull the fake card trick again,
so Sherlock calls his brother who provides

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:15.333
him with access to Baskerville again.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.650
He plans to distract the Major as soon as
they get inside.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:22.630
Then, he wants John to check all the labs
for the glowing hound.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:27.330
John is investigating the labs, and goes further
in the labs than they did last time.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.500
Suddenly, a lab light flashes onto his eyes.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.229
He hears a ringing noise.

00:07:32.229 --> 00:07:35.400
The light keeps on shining brighter and the
ringing gets worse.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.030
John tries to get out of the place but his
key card stops working.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:42.150
Suddenly, the lights go off and the ringing
stops.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.789
The room is pitch dark.

00:07:43.789 --> 00:07:46.870
John then hears a noise and looks for it around
the lab.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.960
He notices a broken cage.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.550
Some animal might have broken out.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.180
Just then he hears a growl.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.889
He runs to the door again and uses his card
but to no avail.

00:07:55.889 --> 00:08:00.690
The growling starts to get louder so he locks
himself in a cage to save him from the animal.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.660
Just then, Sherlock calls him.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.759
He frantically tells Sherlock to come and
save him.

00:08:05.759 --> 00:08:09.840
Sherlock asks him if he can see the hound,
John answers that he does.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.790
Just then, Sherlock turns the lights on and
lets John out.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:17.340
John tries to explain to Sherlock that he
saw the hound, but Sherlock dismisses him,

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.240
saying that he was drugged.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.000
Sherlock then goes to see another doctor from
the lab, Dr. Stapleton.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.820
He borrows her microscope, and studies the
sugar from earlier.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:30.349
Sherlock suspects that they have been drugged
to see the product of their imagination, that

00:08:30.349 --> 00:08:31.560
is the hound.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:35.870
He and Henry both had tea at Henry’s home,
before they went to the hollow that day.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:39.610
He believes that the sugar they put into the
tea was drugged, because both Henry and he

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.709
saw the hound but John did not.

00:08:41.709 --> 00:08:44.430
And John had not taken sugar with his tea.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:48.510
Before coming to Baskerville, Sherlock has
given John coffee with the same sugar in it.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:51.370
Hence, he hallucinated the hound in the lab.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:56.300
However, as he checks the sugar, he can find
no trace of a narcotic.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.150
Agitated, he throws it to the wall.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:01.800
He then uses a mind technique that he likes
to call the ‘mind palace’.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:06.160
While meditating, he deduces that ‘Liberty’
and ‘in’, actually mean Liberty Indiana;

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:10.310
and HOUND was a project at a CIA facility
in Liberty, Indiana.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:14.620
After accessing confidential files, Sherlock
finally realizes the truth.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.490
The project HOUND was established twenty years
ago in Indiana by a group of five researchers.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.320
They had developed a new drug, intended to
be used as a weapon to disorientate the enemy.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.720
However, the project was shut down because
of what it did to the subjects it was tested on.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:33.320
It made the subject extremely violent, causing
many homicides.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:36.470
The same drug had been given to Henry to make
him hallucinate.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:40.790
The entire project was abandoned, but someone
has started it up again.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:45.450
As Sherlock brainstorms who would do this,
he realizes that it is Dr. Frankland.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.830
He has been in the field for a long time.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:52.380
Moreover, Sherlock had picked up on his American
dialect; Dr. Frankland was in Indiana when

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.230
project Hound was running.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:58.040
His obsession with the drug did not change
after moving to the UK.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:02.829
Meanwhile, Henry is in his therapy session
with Louise when suddenly he fires at her,

00:10:02.829 --> 00:10:04.490
hallucinating that she is the hound.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:05.940
Thankfully he misses.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:10.660
As he gets back to his senses, he realizes
what he has done; he apologizes to the doctor

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:13.320
and runs away taking the gun with him.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:17.700
Just then, John gets a call from Louise who
informs him of Henry’s outburst earlier.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.579
She informs that Henry has gone out with a
gun.

00:10:20.579 --> 00:10:23.790
Sherlock deduces that he must have gone to
the Dewer’s Hollow.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:28.700
When Sherlock and John reach there, Henry
is inside the pit, trying to kill himself.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:32.690
Sherlock manages to talk him out of it, explaining
that the hound was a hallucination; Henry's

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:37.370
father was killed not by a devilish hound,
but by Frankland, who was wearing a gas mask

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:41.750
with red-coloured lenses and a sweater with
the words "HOUND" and "Liberty In" on it.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.050
Henry finally comes back to his senses.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.500
But just then, the place starts to fog.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.510
A huge hound appears on top of the pit.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.540
Lestrade is there too.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:55.280
The four start to panic, when Sherlock suddenly
sees Dr Frankland there.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:58.209
Sherlock realizes that the fog was drugged
the whole time.

00:10:58.209 --> 00:11:02.589
They kill the hound, and as the fog clears
up, Henry looks at the hound and realizes

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:04.750
that it is just an ordinary dog.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:07.370
The fog had made them hallucinate.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:11.250
Sherlock explains that pressure pads are installed
around the hollow, which released a dose of

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:14.880
the chemical compound, dosing Henry each time
he visited.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:19.529
With Henry unstable and delirious, his credibility
was damaged, meaning his father's death and

00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:23.230
the dubious experiments at Baskerville could
be covered up...

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:27.329
Henry realises that Frankland murdered his
father, because his father had found him continue

00:11:27.329 --> 00:11:29.250
testing the drug on people.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:34.170
He flies into a vengeful rage and attempts
to throttle Frankland, but the doctor escapes.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:38.860
After a brief chase, Frankland runs into the
Baskerville minefield and steps on a mine,

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:41.050
killing himself in the explosion.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:45.220
The next day, Sherlock and John are having
coffee, discussing the case.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.279
John is confused as to why he saw the hound
in the lab, despite not having inhaled the

00:11:49.279 --> 00:11:51.120
gas from the Moor.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.700
Sherlock tries to explain that the pipes in
the lab must have been leaking the gas, but

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:58.720
John correctly guesses that it was Sherlock
who trapped him in the Baskerville lab; the

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:03.360
terrifying noises made by the 'hound' were
actually just sound effects played in by Sherlock,

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:08.060
as he attempted to test his theory; that the
hallucinogenic drugs had been planted in Henry's sugar

00:12:08.782 --> 00:12:12.682
John also purposely reminds Sherlock of being
wrong when he previously deduced the drug

00:12:12.682 --> 00:12:17.449
was in the sugar, which hits Sherlock's nerves;
he implies he won't get it wrong again another time.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:22.910
At the last scene, we see Sherlock approaching
the innkeeper, implying that the innkeeper

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:27.080
lied about having his dog put down, it was
indeed his dog that the drugged Sherlock and

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.680
the others had perceived as the terrifying
beast.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.269
Subscribe for more videos like this, turn
on notifications, and leave a like to help

00:12:33.269 --> 00:12:34.269
the channel out.

00:12:34.804 --> 00:12:35.720
Thank you for watching.

